Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:06.00,Default,,0,0,0,,We introduce CAST, which improves robot skills while keeping the original\Npolicy as a reference.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.00,0:00:11.00,Default,,0,0,0,,This matters because the critic can misjudge which actions are better.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.00,0:00:15.00,Default,,0,0,0,,As orange shows, even small updates can drift away.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.00,0:00:18.00,Default,,0,0,0,,CAST pulls back, as green shows.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.00,0:00:23.00,Default,,0,0,0,,So we keep the original policy fixed and learn a correction.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.00,0:00:26.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Each action keeps its own reference.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.00,0:00:28.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Here’s one learning step.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.00,0:00:31.00,Default,,0,0,0,,We first sample paired actions.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.00,0:00:37.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Next, the critic proposes an improvement. We normalize, cap, and scale its\Ngradient.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.00,0:00:40.00,Default,,0,0,0,,We also pull toward the base,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.00,0:00:44.00,Default,,0,0,0,,with a stronger pull beyond the reference radius.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.00,0:00:50.00,Default,,0,0,0,,We combine these arrows and cap the target step around the current action.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.00,0:00:54.00,Default,,0,0,0,,We then fit the correction to these fixed targets,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.00,0:00:56.00,Default,,0,0,0,,and repeat the process.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.00,0:01:01.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The policy now learns to match the fixed green targets.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.00,0:01:03.00,Default,,0,0,0,,We refresh them and repeat,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.00,0:01:06.00,Default,,0,0,0,,while the soft pull leaves room to improve.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.00,0:01:12.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Now let’s look at the experiments. In LIBERO, both policies start from the\Nsame state.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.00,0:01:17.00,Default,,0,0,0,,CAST places the bottle in the drawer; the base fails.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.00,0:01:21.00,Default,,0,0,0,,To see how learning progresses, robomimic compares three CAST checkpoints.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.00,0:01:27.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The early policy struggles, while later checkpoints complete the nut\Ninsertion.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.00,0:01:38.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Beyond manipulation, DMC tests locomotion with dense rewards. As CAST\Nlearns, the walker progresses from unsteady movement toward running.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.00,0:01:41.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The measured results show the same pattern.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.00,0:01:50.00,Default,,0,0,0,,In robomimic square, CAST reaches ninety percent success using thirty-eight\Npercent fewer environment steps than DICE-RL.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.00,0:01:55.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Across five LIBERO tasks, no controls or clipping alone gives zero success,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.00,0:01:59.00,Default,,0,0,0,,while CAST improves every task over the base.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.00,0:02:04.00,Default,,0,0,0,,We next move from simulation to OpenArm, using chest and wrist cameras.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.00,0:02:10.00,Default,,0,0,0,,CAST learns offline from recorded successes and failures before deployment.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.00,0:02:15.00,Default,,0,0,0,,We now show the CAST policies completing placement and stacking.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.00,0:02:20.00,Default,,0,0,0,,For placement, the robot reaches down and grasps Jigglypuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.00,0:02:23.00,Default,,0,0,0,,It carries the toy over the case,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.00,0:02:26.00,Default,,0,0,0,,then releases it fully inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.00,0:02:30.00,Default,,0,0,0,,For stacking, it grasps the red cube,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.00,0:02:34.00,Default,,0,0,0,,then aligns it above the purple cube.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.00,0:02:37.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The gripper opens, completing the stack.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.00,0:02:44.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Looking at the overall results, CAST raises placement success from 55 to 95\Npercent.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.00,0:02:51.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Stacking improves from 35 to 70 percent, again exceeding both refinement\Nbaselines.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.00,0:02:55.00,Default,,0,0,0,,In short, we guide improvement, limit each target step,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.00,0:02:59.00,Default,,0,0,0,,and keep the original skill as a reference.
